-- ============================================================================
-- SC2 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Procurement, Tendering & Contracting, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, and the question rows from the
-- committed bank JSONs under tools/course-banks/procurement/beginner.
--
-- What this tier owns: TWO ENVELOPES, BY HAND. What a tender evaluation
-- decides and the sources with their editions and read dates; mandatory
-- requirements, weights, the technical percentage and the pass mark;
-- arithmetic correction with the unit rate prevailing and a misplaced decimal
-- point; the evaluated cost with its discount, deviations, omissions at the
-- average and the completion-time adjustment; the combined score; the ranking,
-- its tie-break and every exclusion. Digest sections 1 to 10, and section 25.
--
-- AN ENGINE COURSE. There is no Suite app: the practicals run in the course's
-- own envelope calculator. The Associate capstone grades six Associate
-- quantities and grades no life-cycle cost, no content figure and no contract
-- comparison.
-- ============================================================================

values ('procurement', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-a-tender-evaluation-decides","title":"What a Tender Evaluation Decides","lesson_keys":["l01-a-scope-a-tender-and-a-contract","l02-one-envelope-then-the-other","l03-the-ekene-tenders","l04-sources-and-the-dates-they-were-read","l05-calculator-panels-and-refusals"]},{"key":"m02-the-technical-envelope","title":"The Technical Envelope","lesson_keys":["l01-mandatory-requirements-first","l02-weights-and-maximum-scores","l03-the-technical-percentage","l04-the-pass-mark-and-the-bid-on-it","l05-a-price-never-opened"]},{"key":"m03-arithmetic-correction","title":"Arithmetic Correction","lesson_keys":["l01-quantity-times-unit-rate","l02-the-unit-rate-prevails","l03-a-misplaced-decimal-point","l04-the-tolerance-and-the-quoted-total"]},{"key":"m04-evaluated-cost","title":"Evaluated Cost","lesson_keys":["l01-corrected-price-less-discount","l02-priced-deviations","l03-an-omitted-item-at-the-average","l04-completion-time-adjustment"]},{"key":"m05-the-combined-score","title":"The Combined Score","lesson_keys":["l01-the-commercial-score","l02-the-relative-technical-score","l03-weighting-the-two-scores","l04-the-guidance-worked-example"]},{"key":"m06-reading-an-award","title":"Reading an Award","lesson_keys":["l01-the-ranking-and-its-tie-break","l02-the-most-advantageous-bid","l03-exclusions-and-their-reasons","l04-the-capstone-brief"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
